# Project:   dfe-docker
# File:      .dockerignore
# Purpose:   Build-context allowlist for docker/dfe-docker.Dockerfile, the one build with this repo root as its context
# Language:  dockerignore
#
# License:   BUSL-1.1
# Copyright: (c) 2026 HYPERI PTY LIMITED
#
# The dfe-docker image copies its whole context into the folder `init` sets up,
# so this names what that folder holds and nothing more. An allowlist, because
# a file nobody listed then stays out: .env, env/, certs/ and access-summary.md
# hold secrets and can never reach an image layer.
#
# scripts/build_dev_images.py stages each component's source into its own temp
# context, so this file does not reach those builds.

*

!.env.example
!Makefile
!VERSION
!LICENSE
!compose/
!config/
!deployment.example.yaml
!docker-compose.yml
!docker/dfe-docker.requirements.txt
!env.example/
!redpanda/
!resources/
!scripts/
!service_profiles.yaml

# Inside the kept directories: tests and bytecode never run in a deployment
scripts/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
